---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../../components/Hero.astro";
import Button from "../../components/Button.astro";
import CaseStudyCard from "../../components/CaseStudyCard.astro";
import TechUsage from "../../components/TechUsage.astro";
import "../../styles/markdown.css";

import DailySelfTrackScreenshots from "../../assets/images/portfolio/DailySelfTrack-Main-Screenshots.png";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Portfolio - Bryan Hogan"
    description="Bryan Hogan designs and builds digital products, from user research to shipped code. Case studies of DailySelfTrack and Sorbit, and the tech behind them."
>
    <Hero heading="Portfolio" headingDetail="Work and experience by Bryan Hogan" />

    <div class="markdown-container margin-top-xl margin-inline-auto">
        <p>
            I start from what people need and work backwards to the design and the technology that gets them there. I research the problem with users and define what's worth solving. From there I work in an iterative, user-centered design process: design, prototype, test and iterate, before and during development.
        </p>
        <p>
            I studied <a href="/blog/what-is-coco">Code &amp; Context</a> at TH Köln, a degree that combines <strong>computer science</strong>, <strong>design</strong> and <strong>entrepreneurship</strong>. I've also worked as a software developer, in online marketing and in social media management. So I also think about the business side of a product, like market fit, marketing and the journey from first interaction to long-term use.
        </p>
        <p>
            My largest freelance project was Sorbit, an app for a psychology start-up. For other clients I've built business automations and company websites, such as <a href="https://www.fch-dachdecker.de/">FCH Dachdecker</a>. My own products include <a href="https://dailyselftrack.com/">DailySelfTrack</a>, a self-tracking app that started as my bachelor thesis, <a href="https://starter.bryanhogan.com/">StarStarter for Astro</a> and the <a href="https://webdev.bryanhogan.com/">Clean Web Development Guide</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="intro-actions margin-inline-auto">
        <div class="cta-row">
            <Button href="mailto:bryan@bryanhogan.com" size="medium" iconLeft="email">Email</Button>
            <Button href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/bryanhoganme/" variant="secondary" size="medium" target="_blank" iconLeft="linkedin">LinkedIn</Button>
        </div>
        <p class="aside">
            Just here for my projects or writing instead? See my <a href="/projects">projects</a> and <a href="/blog">blog</a>.
        </p>
    </div>

    <section class="wide-section margin-top-2xl margin-inline-auto">
        <h2>Case studies</h2>
        <div class="case-study-list">
            <CaseStudyCard
                title="DailySelfTrack"
                description="A self-tracking app that combines the flexibility of a spreadsheet with the usability of a dedicated app. I took it from bachelor thesis research through user tests and two rebuilds to a local-first app that works offline."
                caseStudyHref="/portfolio/dailyselftrack"
                liveHref="https://app.dailyselftrack.com/"
                liveText="Try the app"
                image={DailySelfTrackScreenshots}
                imageAlt="DailySelfTrack screenshots showing three different views on a vibrant gradient background"
            />
            <CaseStudyCard
                title="Sorbit"
                description="An app for keeping in touch with the people closest to you, built as a freelancer for a psychology start-up. I built the app and shared the UX work with the founder."
                caseStudyHref="/portfolio/sorbit"
                liveHref="https://sorbit.app/"
                liveText="Website"
            >
                <svg slot="visual" viewBox="0 0 200 200" role="img" aria-label="Simple orbit graphic: a center dot surrounded by three rings with small dots on them">
                    <g fill="none" style="stroke: var(--color-neutral-500)" stroke-width="1.5">
                        <circle cx="100" cy="100" r="30" />
                        <circle cx="100" cy="100" r="55" />
                        <circle cx="100" cy="100" r="80" />
                    </g>
                    <circle cx="100" cy="100" r="14" style="fill: var(--color-accent-500)" />
                    <g style="fill: var(--color-accent-200)">
                        <circle cx="119.3" cy="77" r="6" />
                        <circle cx="48.3" cy="118.8" r="5" />
                        <circle cx="151.7" cy="118.8" r="5" />
                        <circle cx="60" cy="30.7" r="4" />
                        <circle cx="140" cy="169.3" r="4" />
                    </g>
                </svg>
            </CaseStudyCard>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wide-section margin-top-2xl margin-inline-auto">
        <h2>Skills and tools</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Select one to see how and where I've used it.</p>
        <TechUsage />
    </section>

    <div class="markdown-container margin-top-2xl margin-bottom-xl margin-inline-auto">
        <h2>Experience and education</h2>
        <p>
            I graduated in Cologne, worked freelance while living in South Korea, Macau, Japan and Australia, and am now back in Germany looking for a full-time position. I am a German and British citizen. I speak German and English. My Korean is at around A2 to B1 level.
        </p>

        <h3>Education</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>B.Sc. Code &amp; Context</strong> at TH Köln (Cologne University of Applied Sciences)
                <ul>
                    <li>Bachelor thesis: Does greater customization in a self-tracking app improve usability and market fit?</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Exchange semester</strong> at Hanyang University ERICA in Ansan, South Korea</li>
            <li><strong>Exchange semester</strong> at the University of Seoul in Seoul, South Korea</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Work</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Freelance web app developer and designer</strong> at Webagentur Hogan, remote</li>
            <li><strong>Research intern</strong> at the University of Macau</li>
            <li><strong>Software developer</strong> at Digital Solution Group GmbH in Germany</li>
            <li><strong>Online marketing and website management</strong> at Handon dressed to sell GmbH in Cologne</li>
            <li><strong>Social media management</strong> at Volt Deutschland in Germany</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You can find more details about my work experience on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/bryanhoganme/">LinkedIn</a>.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
            I'm open to full-time roles and to relocating internationally. Email me at <a href="mailto:bryan@bryanhogan.com">bryan@bryanhogan.com</a> or reach me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/bryanhoganme/">LinkedIn</a> and my other <a href="/socials">socials</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .cta-row {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: var(--space-s);
    }
    .intro-actions {
        width: 100%;
        max-width: min(100%, var(--main-content-max-width));
        margin-top: var(--space-m);
    }
    .aside {
        margin-top: var(--space-s);
        font-size: var(--font-size-small);
        color: var(--color-neutral-300);
        & a {
            font-size: inherit;
            color: var(--a-hover-color);
        }
    }
    .wide-section {
        max-width: 64rem;
        width: 100%;
        & h2 {
            margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
        }
    }
    .section-intro {
        color: var(--color-neutral-300);
        margin-top: calc(var(--space-s) * -1);
        margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
    }
    .case-study-list {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: var(--space-l);
    }
</style>
